// expect-error: NITPICK-MACRO-007
// expect-error-at: 23:5
// expect-note: NITPICK-MACRO-009
// expect-note-at: 26:1
//
// TWO MODULES' MACROS CANNOT FORM A CYCLE (D-124; DEF-172, 1.6.1e step 3). `here`
// invokes `there` and, in `lib/cycle_peer.npk`, `there` invokes `here` -- by name,
// a ring. But a macro is invocable only in the module that declares it, so
// neither invocation names a macro of ITS OWN module, the cycle check reads no
// edge from either body, and there is NO `NITPICK-MACRO-004` in this file.
//
// What is wrong is the reach, and it is reported as that: `#here()` expands, its
// body's `#there()` names a macro of another module, MACRO-007 -- at the
// invocation inside the body, with the note that says which invocation of `here`
// brought it. The set of codes this file reports is exactly {MACRO-007}; a cycle
// check that looked across modules would add a second code and fail it.
mod:cycle_cross_module;

use "./lib/cycle_peer.npk".*;

macro:here = () {
    func:from_here = int32() never fails { pass 1i32; };
    #there();
};

#here();

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    int32:a = raw peer_anchor();
    exit 0i32;
};
